WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.410
- You saw me sing with my next
guest earlier in the show.

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:05.290
He's one of the most talented artists

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:06.470
in country music today.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:09.310
His latest album is called
"Sunday Drive" and it's out now.

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:10.900
You should get it if you're cool.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.863
Give it up for Brett Eldredge, everybody.

00:00:12.863 --> 00:00:15.863
(audience cheering)

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:30.760
I know, it's so weird.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.460
I have guests here and I can't hug them.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:33.930
- I know, I love hugging too.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:34.763
- I know me too.

00:00:34.763 --> 00:00:36.344
It's like a southern thing,
I guess, I don't know.

00:00:36.344 --> 00:00:38.263
- [Brett] I'm making myself
at home, is that cool?

00:00:38.263 --> 00:00:39.703
- Yes, I actually we were discussing this-

00:00:39.703 --> 00:00:42.130
- Can I have this couch when we're done?

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.877
- It's a really cool couch.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.213
It's a lovely color of it.
- It's awesome.

00:00:45.213 --> 00:00:46.550
I got the red and the green right here.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:47.383
I feel very festive.
- I know.

00:00:47.383 --> 00:00:49.050
You're very Christmasy, yes.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.668
Well, thank you for singing with me.

00:00:50.668 --> 00:00:51.550
- Are you kidding?

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:52.383
It was amazing.

00:00:52.383 --> 00:00:53.870
- I was very excited.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.810
You can ask Shane, our friend,
we have a mutual friend.

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:57.920
And we were talking about it earlier,

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.340
that we hadn't met until today,

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:02.700
and so we had to record it
separate, or separately rather.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:03.810
But have you ever done that?

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.423
Have you ever recorded a duet?

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.450
- I did with Meghan Trainor.

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:10.180
- [Kelly] You never met her and you never?

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:13.535
- No, I knew her, but we
were in the middle of tour.

00:01:13.535 --> 00:01:16.640
And we did "Baby, It's Cold Outside."

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:18.715
- Oh my gosh, I love that song.

00:01:18.715 --> 00:01:20.790
- And it was awesome.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:22.530
But, yeah, we knew each
other, but we never-

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:23.751
- But you had at least met.

00:01:23.751 --> 00:01:25.826
- Yeah, I've never done it like this.

00:01:25.826 --> 00:01:29.467
- I know, I don't know if
I've ever not met the person.

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:31.555
- But I met you, when I
heard your voice, I was like,

00:01:31.555 --> 00:01:32.396
♪ Ah ♪

00:01:32.396 --> 00:01:33.830
And then we sang, it was awesome.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:36.000
- Same, what are like your...

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.370
Like for me to know it's Christmas

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.527
is hearing Bing Crosby's
"White Christmas."

00:01:40.527 --> 00:01:42.252
And I heard that that's
one of your favorites.

00:01:42.252 --> 00:01:46.030
- That's the song, the cassette.

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:47.915
So my dad had the
cassette back in the day.

00:01:47.915 --> 00:01:48.810
- [Kelly] A cassette.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:50.730
- You know, I'd go to
the glove compartment.

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:54.710
It's about, you know,
November, around right now.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:57.770
And you just open that glove compartment

00:01:57.770 --> 00:01:59.420
and there's Bing Crosby's
"White Christmas."

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:01.750
And I popped it in there as a little kid.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:04.640
And I'm listening to this
old man sing his heart out.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.813
And it just like,

00:02:06.813 --> 00:02:08.240
I think that's when I got my old soul.

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.190
Like I feel like I had an old soul.

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:11.350
And that's when I started
loving Christmas music

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:12.360
and the magic of it.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.020
And Bing Crosby just did it for me.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:17.880
- Okay, so mine was not only Bing Crosby,

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:18.713
but Rosemary Clooney,

00:02:18.713 --> 00:02:21.098
because they were both
in "White Christmas."

00:02:21.098 --> 00:02:22.180
I was obsessed.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:24.620
- Probably my favorite movie.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:25.730
- All right, well, the title track

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:28.460
on Brett's new album, "Sunday
Drive," is about his family.

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:31.880
He sings, "It's the ordinary
things that means so much.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.060
That's where I learned it all from them.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:36.870
To fight, to love, to laugh again.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.790
Man, I thought we were only wasting time

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.300
out on the 'Sunday Drive.'"

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:43.760
I like the simplicity of that lyric

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.720
and what it represents for so many people.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:46.830
And you did, you thought it was just

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.650
kind of like we're wasting time.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:50.720
- Yeah, I mean, I still go back

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:53.690
to like after a baseball game as a kid

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:55.323
eating Dairy Queen in
the back of the car like,

00:02:55.323 --> 00:02:58.210
and spilling cookie dough
blizzard all over myself.

00:02:58.210 --> 00:02:59.150
- But that's so beautiful.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:00.037
Those are those nostalgic moments.

00:03:00.037 --> 00:03:02.600
- You think those moments are,

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.320
you know, you don't
realize it at the moment.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:05.350
And the next thing you know,

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:07.230
you get older and you're in high school

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:08.230
and rolling the windows down,

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:09.880
and the music's blaring
and you feel alive.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:11.550
And then next thing you know,

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:14.570
you're grown up and you
realize how quick time goes.

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:16.420
And it's making the moments count

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.720
and with the ones you love, so.

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.470
- Totally, and it really hits you

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:21.480
I think when you pass those places.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:22.470
It's like you pass a Dairy Queen,

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:23.996
or you smell a certain scent
that reminds you of something.

00:03:23.996 --> 00:03:25.460
- Oh, right back.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:29.100
- Yeah, it's a really cool
idea for a song, clever.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.080
I heard you took a very different approach

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:32.060
to writing this record.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.050
You kind of like went off the grid,

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:34.883
right?
- Yeah.

00:03:34.883 --> 00:03:36.130
- Yeah.
- So I-

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:37.360
- Like how off the grid?

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.640
- I was heavily on all the
social media and everything,

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:42.780
and just constantly on my phone.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:46.100
And I was like, "I gotta just
step away from everything.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.700
Take some time for myself."

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:48.680
I got a flip phone.

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:49.920
- A flip phone.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.030
Like, wait, oh my gosh.
- Yeah, I mean,

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.630
straight up hang up on somebody
and close it, you know.

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:54.463
Make a point kind of thing.

00:03:54.463 --> 00:03:55.910
- The only thing better
would've been a beeper.

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:57.130
But okay.
- Yeah, that's next.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:59.430
That's my next stage for my next album.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:01.490
But it just really made me kind of focus

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:02.580
on myself for a while

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:03.990
and just kind of figure
out what I wanted to say,

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:04.823
who I wanted to be.

00:04:04.823 --> 00:04:06.390
I started journaling a lot more.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:07.450
I got a Polaroid camera.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:09.240
I was taking photos actually
making every one count.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.141
Every picture wasn't perfect.

00:04:10.141 --> 00:04:11.780
You know, when you have a phone you're,

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:13.980
you can take 4,000 pictures and pick one.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.910
It's like Polaroid, you
gotta make that moment count.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:18.530
So just doing stuff like
that really made me,

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:19.750
you know, reflective of my life,

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:21.866
where I was, and where I am,
and where I wanna go with it.

00:04:21.866 --> 00:04:22.933
- Slow it down and appreciate it.

00:04:22.933 --> 00:04:24.618
- Slow it down, yep.

00:04:24.618 --> 00:04:25.451
- [Kelly] So I think that's
why I love this record so much.

00:04:25.451 --> 00:04:26.680
- There's never a moment for yourself.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:28.660
- It feels real, like a real album.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:29.680
- Yes, well thank you.

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:31.570
- Yeah, and actually,

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.530
I think it was Blake and
or Gwen, one of them,

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:35.630
is the one who turned
me on to it at first.

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:36.550
And I was like, "Oh."

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:37.660
I was like, "I gotta check that out."

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:40.460
But it's really well done as in an album.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:41.509
It sounds like an album.
- Well, thank you.

00:04:41.509 --> 00:04:42.430
- Yeah.
- Well, I appreciate that.

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:43.720
- Yeah, well done.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:46.270
Well, Brett's album, "Sunday
Drive," is available now.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:47.920
If you're cool, you'll go get it.

